# Pre-existing environment gap (NOT this ticket's code): a fresh /new-task worktree has no
# UserApp/android/app/google-services.json (gitignored) and, more specifically, the PRIMARY
# tree's copy only registers the base package_name "com.izzes.nears" — a worktree's
# NEARS-1808-suffixed applicationId (com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_3625_checkout_uiux here) has
# no matching client entry, so Firebase.initializeApp() throws [core/no-app] app-wide.
# This is caught safely everywhere EXCEPT LocationController._saveDataAndFirebaseConfig ->
# LocationService.configureFirebaseMessaging (location_service.dart:151), which calls
# FirebaseMessaging.instance UNGUARDED (not through AnalyticsService's safe _analytics getter) —
# an uncaught synchronous throw inside an un-awaited call that ABORTS the rest of
# LocationController.autoNavigate, permanently stranding first-run users on the pick-location
# screen (get-zone-id succeeds, inZone=true, but navigation never completes):
#
09-18 04:01:00.498 E flutter : [ERROR:flutter/runtime/dart_vm_initializer.cc(40)] Unhandled Exception: [core/no-app] No Firebase App '[DEFAULT]' has been created - call Firebase.initializeApp()
09-18 04:01:00.498 E flutter : #3      LocationService.configureFirebaseMessaging (package:nears/features/location/domain/services/location_service.dart:151:25)
09-18 04:01:00.498 E flutter : #4      LocationController._saveDataAndFirebaseConfig (package:nears/features/location/controllers/location_controller.dart:1133:30)
09-18 04:01:00.498 E flutter : #5      LocationController.autoNavigate (package:nears/features/location/controllers/location_controller.dart:991:14)
#
# Same shape as the already-known NEARS-957 finding (DeliveryApp/VendorApp Firebase cold-start
# crash without google-services.json) but a DIFFERENT call site (UserApp's LocationController,
# not app boot) and a harder failure mode (silently stuck screen, not a crash).
# Workaround used to unblock this QA run (local, non-committed, non-code): copied the primary
# tree's google-services.json into the worktree and appended a second `client[]` entry cloning
# the existing one with package_name replaced by this worktree's suffixed id, then did a full
# `flutter run` (Gradle re-processes google-services.json at build time). Not a product fix —
# flagging for the ai-engineer/workflow-tooling owner per NEARS-957's precedent.
